      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that you are the problem is a heavy, but ultimately untrue, narrative you've been telling yourself. The damage you perceive is often a reflection of your own pain, not a permanent stain on your worth. Instead of trying to stop the cycle, consider what small, manageable step you could take today to ease the pressure, even if it's just for yourself. Reaching out to a professional can help you untangle these feelings of guilt and worthlessness.",
      "source": "target",
